# Trivy vulnerability suppressions.
#
# Each entry must document WHY the finding is not applicable. Re-review on every
# dependency bump and remove the entry once it can be resolved upstream.

# CVE-2026-34040 — github.com/docker/docker (Moby authorization bypass)
#
# Revalidated 2026-10-03 at 78dc97bf4642c7822d737c2a126c48d792eb1ccd:
#   * go mod why -m github.com/docker/docker traces the dependency through
#     golang-migrate/migrate/v4/database/postgres.test -> dhui/dktest.
#     It is retained for an upstream dependency's tests, not imported by this
#     application's code or tests. Testcontainers v0.44.0 uses moby/moby/client.
#   * go list -deps -test ./... finds no docker/docker packages for the release
#     targets (linux, windows, darwin; amd64 and arm64; CGO_ENABLED=0).
#   * This advisory concerns the Docker daemon's AuthZ request-body handling.
#     Neither the daemon nor its authorization middleware is linked here.
#     This exception does not establish the safety of external Docker hosts.
#   * The Go advisory has no fixed release on the legacy docker/docker path.
#     Its moby/moby/v2 fix is v2.0.0-beta.8, a different module, not a drop-in
#     version bump. Even migrate v4.20.1 retains docker/docker via dktest.
#     Revisit if the import graph changes or migrate/dktest removes the module.
#   * Evidence: https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-4887
#     https://github.com/moby/moby/security/advisories/GHSA-x744-4wpc-v9h2
CVE-2026-34040
